<p>You do not need an expensive dinner to have a good first meeting. The best first date ideas in Nairobi are simple, public and relaxed, and they give you something to look at and talk about besides each other. This guide shares free and budget-friendly options, from daytime coffee to forest walks, plus a few practical tips so you feel safe and prepared.</p>
<p>A quick note on money: prices change and every place sets its own, so costs vary. We have not listed any prices here. Check entry fees, opening times and menus before you go, and agree on a plan you can both afford.</p>

<h2>What makes a good first date</h2>
<p>A good first date has three qualities. It is in a public place, it is short, and it is easy to leave. You are meeting someone you know mostly through messages, so the goal is simply to see whether you enjoy each other's company in real life.</p>
<p>Activities that give you something to do together tend to work better than a long sit-down meal. Walking or looking around takes the pressure off eye contact, and the surroundings give you natural topics when conversation slows down. Keep the plan to one or two hours. If it goes well, you can always stay longer.</p>

<h2>Daytime coffee or tea in a busy spot</h2>
<p>The classic for a reason. A coffee, tea or fresh juice at a busy cafe in daylight is low cost, easy to arrange and easy to end politely. Choose a place with other customers, a clear entrance, and good light. Many malls and town centres around Nairobi have such spots.</p>
<ul>
<li>Pick a time when the place is lively, such as mid-morning or early afternoon.</li>
<li>Arrive a few minutes early so you can choose a seat you like.</li>
