<h2>Museums, galleries and cultural spaces</h2>
<p>Museums and galleries are a great way to turn quiet moments into conversation. You can comment on what you see, ask what each other finds interesting, and learn something about their taste without any pressure. Nairobi has museums, art spaces and cultural centres that are open to the public, and many are in busy areas that are easy to reach by matatu, ride-hailing or on foot.</p>
<p>Opening hours and entry fees vary, so check ahead. Some places have cheaper rates for residents or students, and some have free days or events. If you are not sure, a quick call or message before you go will save an awkward moment at the gate.</p>

